    <Folder>
      <name>High-end Restaurants</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Osteria Piazzetta Cattedrale</name>
        <description>In Ostuni
Modern Apulian
Price: Around €35 – €50.
The best table in the White City; incredible local pasta.
Note: This is considered one of the best bargains in the guide; it feels like a starred meal at a fraction of the price.
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>17.57835,40.73425,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Meraviglioso</name>
        <description>In Polignano a Mare
Contemporary Seafood
Price: Around €90 for a full tasting; €45 – €55 if eating à la carte.
High-end seafood in a town famous for it.
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>17.21719,40.99706,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>L'Antica Locanda</name>
        <description>In Noci
Traditional
Noci is the &quot;town of food&quot;; this spot is famous for local meats.
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>17.12268,40.79625,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>DolceVita</name>
        <description>In Gallipoli
Seafood / View
Located on the rooftop of Palazzo del Corso with harbor views.
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>17.98408,40.05604,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>L'Altro Baffo</name>
        <description>In Otranto
Modern Seafood
Price: €65 (5 courses) to €85 (7 courses).
Famous for &quot;Carbonara di Pesce&quot; (fish carbonara).
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>18.49154,40.14502,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Osteria Sant'Agostino</name>
        <description>In Gravina in Puglia
Rustic/Stone
Price: €35 – €50.
Very rustic and value-driven.
Focuses on the &quot;Murgia&quot; flavors (lamb, mushrooms, wild greens).
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>16.41602,40.81602,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>L'Antica Locanda</name>
        <description>In Lecce
Price: €45 – €60
Famous for its &quot;succession of appetizers&quot; which can be a meal in itself.
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>18.17061,40.35440,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Antichi Sapori</name>
        <description>In Montegrosso
Near Castel del Monte
Price: €50 for a massive, multi-course traditional feast.
Note: This is a &quot;cult&quot; favorite. There is no menu; you eat what Pietro Zito harvested from the garden that morning.
</description>
        <styleUrl>#paddle-blu-circle</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>16.14110,41.17231,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
